emics Academic Programs Anthrozoology Business Management Hospitality and Tourism Computer Information Systems Design and Digital Media Early Childhood and Elementary Education Humanities Human Services Psychology Studio Arts Minors Success & Support Services Academic Advising Academic Support Career Preparation Career Treks Internships Study Abroad Resources Course Catalog Academic Calendars Registrar’s Office Academics Intellectual challenge is at the heart of a Beacon education. We take this very seriously, but we are also very practical about it. Our 10 bachelor’s degree programs are intended to prepare our students to find worthy work in today’s global marketplace.  Additionally, we encourage students to explore their diverse interests through one or more of our 17 minors. Student Life Campus Life Life at Beacon First Year Experience Housing Dining Services Transportation Health and Wellness Safety Activities Activities and Clubs Fitness and Recreation Athletics Athletics Men’s Basketball Women’s Basketball Cross Country and Track Golf Student Life “Pursuing the life abundant” is the pervading theme that infuses everything we do at Beacon College. It’s something we take very seriously indeed. At Beacon, you’ll be able to be the most that you can be. Both within the classroom and far beyond it, we nurture a vivacious learning laboratory that calls upon you to seek and cherish all of life’s richness. News & Events News & Media News and Updates Lighting the Path Newsletter A World of Difference Office of Communications Events Salon Series Family Weekend Alumni Weekend Commencement News & Events We are committed to keeping you up to date. Check out current news, media, and upcoming events from Beacon College. Search Career Treks Home Academics Career Treks Summer Experiential Learning Program in Leesburg You can participate in Beacon’s intensive career-focused summer program – Career Treks! You’ll be exposed to different career opportunities and embark on field trips to some of Florida’s largest companies and nonprofits. Career Treks provides skills-based learning options and delves into more than simply job titles helping you find your career path. Have Questions? Email the Career Center Internships Career Preparation In the Field Career Trek students explored careers in game development at UCF’s globally ranked Florida Interactive Entertainment Academy where they learned more about the graduate program for a master of science in interactive entertainment. 4Rivers hosted our Career Treks students for behind-the-scenes tours learning about farm to table, regenerative agriculture, biodiversity and most of all giving back to the community. Publix hosted Career Treks students where they learned about opportunities in how their majors could lead them into talent acquisition, brand marketing, real estate development, risk management and compliance. Career Treks students toured an Amazon fulfillment center where they saw firsthand how robotics and AI directly influence nearly every shipment that Amazon is responsible for. About the Program Through this unique experience, you’ll learn about career pipelines for a variety of majors and minors and have a better understanding of the competitive employment market for new graduates. You’ll visit work sites, attend discussion panels, and network with industry professionals throughout Central Florida. Additionally, you’ll be able to explore certifications and microcredentials adding value to your degree. The Career Treks program provides you the opportunity to earn 50% of the 120-hour experiential learning hours required to graduate. Virtual Internship Opportunity New for Career Treks 2026! In addition to the two-week on campus program, we are offering a 12-week virtual internship option. Direct placement in a 12-week virtual internship (completed remotely, off-campus for set hours each day/week.) Program cost includes all internship placement services, ongoing student support/coaching, and progress monitoring by Career Center staff until program concludes. Through the virtual internship option, you will have the opportunity to earn 80+ additional experiential learning hours. What are the dates? May 11-22, 2026 What is the cost? With two program options, costs vary depending on chosen program. Application Requirements Submit the application form by Feb. 27, 2026 Eligibility Open to all Beacon students. Only 40 students in good standing will be accepted. Is transportation provided? All transportation to the employer site visits and other excursions are included. Contact Information Melissa Bradley Executive Director of Center for Career Preparation 352-787-1658 mbradley@beaconcollege.edu Marissa Esty Career Advisor 352-805-1296 mesty@beaconcollege.edu Faith Otero Career Advisor 352-638-9826 fotero@beaconcollege.edu Brianna Rivera Program Assistant 352-638-9808 brivera1@beaconcollege.edu Learn More Learn more about how the Juan and Lisa Jones Center for Career Preparation works with you in career development! Schedule an appointment in Handshake today! Apply Today Request Info Plan a Visit RESOURCES Directory Campus Map Alumni Email Portal MyBeacon Portal Canvas Tech Support For Media WORKING AT BEACON Career Opportunities Faculty/Staff Portal Student Employment Giving Beacon College’s EASE Grant Performance Measures If you’re having accessibility issues, please let us know . Contact Us (855) 220-5374 Address 105 East Main Street Leesburg, Florida 34748 Follow Us © 2026 Beacon College. Web Design by PHOS Creative Sitemap Privacy Policy Accessibility Title VI Title IX"
